  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 328 PM EDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nOn Tuesday, ridging will be centered over the Ohio Valley. Surface \nhigh pressure will keep pushing east, which will promote \nsouthwesterly flow into the region. A low pressure system will move \nthrough southern Canada, which will tighten the pressure gradient \nover the region. Breezy winds, increased moisture, and hot \ntemperatures are expected for Tuesday. Peak heat indices will be 97-\n100F (in the Bluegrass) and 100-106F elsewhere. A heat advisory has \nbeen issued for the western half of the region for Tuesday.\n\nSimilar conditions will last through at least mid week. High \ntemperatures will remain in the mid 90s through Thursday. A heat \nadvisory will likely need to be continued through mid week. Given \nthe time of year, these temperatures and heat indices are unusual \n(about 10-12 degrees above normal). HeatRisk is expected to be Major \n(level 3/4) Tuesday through at least Thursday. NBM (and associated \nguidance) is likely not handling temperatures as well, given decent \nsouthwesterly flow and the beginnings of the transition season. \nTherefore, have bumped temperatures bit a bit, specifically \novernight. Looking at records, we may approach both high \ntemperatures and warm mins this week.\n\nMoving into Friday and the weekend, ridging remains over the \nsouthern CONUS, though multiple shortwaves will attempt to move \nacross the region. This would bring isolated to scattered showers \nand storms and slightly cooler temperatures.",
